## Clear pytest deprecation warnings (utcnow, pyshacl default_context)

Context: The frozen non-scenario suite reported 39 warnings. Two sources:
(1) our `datetime.utcnow()` in TwinBackgroundTasks (deprecated since Python 3.12),
and (2) upstream `Dataset.default_context is deprecated` raised inside pyshacl 0.31
and rdflib 7.6 during SHACL validation. Upgrading pyshacl to 0.40.2 was probed
and still touches `default_context` (clone.py), so the lockfile is left untouched.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py
   New module helper `_utc_now_naive_iso()` (timezone-aware UTC, tzinfo stripped to
   keep the naive ISO shape) replaces `datetime.utcnow()` for `last_run`; drop the
   now-unused local `datetime` import in `run_inference_task`.
2. pytest.ini
   Scoped ignore for the upstream `Dataset.default_context is deprecated` message
   (modules `pyshacl.*` and `rdflib.graph` only).
3. pyproject.toml
   Mirror of the same scoped ignore in `[tool.pytest.ini_options]`.

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py
- pytest.ini
- pyproject.toml
- changelogs/v0.9.3/benoitcayladbx_2026-11-16.log

